# Toy control (D-85, D-55): a run library with state shared by every instance, made from the live src/core/run.c by scripts/control-mutate (plan 03-02 re-pointed it from the deleted
# placeholder stepping). The anchor is the one live line that adds the clocks of a step to the machine time; the replacement folds a hidden function-local static counter into that
# update (every fifth step of the whole process takes one master clock more), so the machine time of an instance depends on how many steps every instance in the process has taken. A
# deliberately aliased toy lives in build/ only, never in src/core (the boundary check bans exactly this in the real core, and no copy of run.c is committed). The interleave cases in
# EXPECT must come out guest_failure on the toy, or they prove nothing about sharing.
tag=rule-shared-counter
file=src/core/run.c
anchor=inst->machine_time = inst->machine_time + (uint64_t)ds_cpu_step_obs(inst, obs);
replace={ static uint64_t shared_n = 0u; inst->machine_time = inst->machine_time + (uint64_t)ds_cpu_step_obs(inst, obs) + (uint64_t)(++shared_n % 5u == 0u); }
